1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,450
Leon: Hi Shannon - how are you settling into your new flat?

2
00:00:03,450 --> 00:00:05,200
Shannon: Really well, thanks.

3
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:08,460
Leon: You look like you're going shopping.

4
00:00:08,460 --> 00:00:11,760
Shannon: Yes, I am. My cousins are coming to stay for a couple of days

5
00:00:11,760 --> 00:00:13,580
and I have to cook for them.

6
00:00:13,580 --> 00:00:17,760
Leon: Well, there are plenty of places to buy food in Kite Place

7
00:00:18,280 --> 00:00:20,620
it's the area by the harbour.

8
00:00:20,620 --> 00:00:25,640
Shannon: Oh, OK, I'll find that on the map. Thanks.

9
00:00:25,640 --> 00:00:28,230
Leon: What sort of food do you need to get?

10
00:00:28,230 --> 00:00:32,240
Shannon: Well, neither of them eats meat but they both like fish.

11
00:00:32,240 --> 00:00:35,190
Leon: Well, there's a really good fish market there.

12
00:00:35,190 --> 00:00:38,140
Shannon: Oh great - where is it exactly?

13
00:00:38,140 --> 00:00:41,316
Leon: It's at the far end of Kite Place,

14
00:00:41,316 --> 00:00:46,080
so you have to go over the bridge and then it's on the right.

15
00:00:46,080 --> 00:00:49,320
Shannon: OK - is it open all day?

16
00:00:49,320 --> 00:00:54,540
Leon: It doesn't close until four, but I'd recommend going earlier than that

17
00:00:54,540 --> 00:00:56,800
it does run out of some things.

18
00:00:56,800 --> 00:00:59,120
Shannon: Oh, I don't want that to happen.

19
00:00:59,120 --> 00:01:03,120
Leon: As long as you get there by 3.30, you should be fine

20
00:01:03,720 --> 00:01:06,310
It's only 11 now, so plenty of time.

21
00:01:06,310 --> 00:01:07,540
Shannon: Right.

22
00:01:07,540 --> 00:01:10,000
Leon: Do you need to buy vegetables too?

23
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:14,810
Shannon: I do, and I want to avoid all the plastic packaging in the supermarket!

24
00:01:14,810 --> 00:01:18,369
Leon: Well, there's a really nice organic shop there.

25
00:01:18,369 --> 00:01:24,420
Now what's it called... it's the name of a flower. I know, it's 'Rose'.

26
00:01:24,420 --> 00:01:25,990
Shannon: That's a nice name.

27
00:01:25,990 --> 00:01:29,940
Leon: Yeah - it sells vegetables and quite a lot of other stuff.

28
00:01:29,940 --> 00:01:31,220
Shannon: And where's that?

29
00:01:31,220 --> 00:01:33,080
Leon: Well, as you reach the market

30
00:01:33,080 --> 00:01:37,068
you'll see a big grey building on your left Leon:

31
00:01:37,068 --> 00:01:39,667
I think it used to be a warehouse.

32
00:01:39,667 --> 00:01:42,053
Anyway, now it's a restaurant upstairs,

33
00:01:42,053 --> 00:01:46,720
but the ground floor has two shops either side of the entrance

34
00:01:46,720 --> 00:01:48,870
and it's the one on the left.

35
00:01:48,870 --> 00:01:50,450
Shannon: That's easy enough.

36
00:01:50,450 --> 00:01:55,080
Leon: You can't miss it - there's also a big sign on the pavement

37
00:01:55,080 --> 00:01:57,090
so you can look for that.

38
00:01:57,090 --> 00:02:02,990
Shannon: Fine! I guess if I need anything else, I'll have to go to the supermarket.

39
00:02:02,990 --> 00:02:07,123
Leon: Yeah - you should be able to get everything you need,

40
00:02:07,123 --> 00:02:12,384
but there's a minibus that goes to the supermarket if you need it.

41
00:02:12,384 --> 00:02:15,390
It's purple and the number is 289.

42
00:02:15,390 --> 00:02:19,660
Shannon: Thanks, that's great.

43
00:02:19,660 --> 00:02:22,540
Leon: So what do you need to get at the fish market

44
00:02:23,120 --> 00:02:27,120
The salmon is always very good and the shellfish.

45
00:02:27,120 --> 00:02:32,600
Shannon: I'm going to make a curry, I think, and I need about 12 prawns for that.

46
00:02:32,600 --> 00:02:33,880
Leon: They'll have plenty of those.

47
00:02:33,880 --> 00:02:35,240
Shannon: OK.

48
00:02:35,240 --> 00:02:37,630
Leon: Have you ever tried samphire?

49
00:02:37,630 --> 00:02:39,580
Shannon: No - what's that?

50
00:02:39,580 --> 00:02:41,420
Leon: It's a type of seaweed

51
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:47,290
I just ask for a handful and you fry it in butter. It's delicious!

52
00:02:47,290 --> 00:02:51,140
Shannon: Oh, I might try that - how do you spell it?

53
00:02:51,140 --> 00:03:01,010
Leon: It's S-A-M-P-H. I-R-E.

54
00:03:01,010 --> 00:03:04,530
Shannon: Great - it's always good to try something different.

55
00:03:04,530 --> 00:03:05,730
Leon: Yeah.

56
00:03:05,730 --> 00:03:09,020
Shannon: I'll see what beans they have in the organic shop

57
00:03:09,020 --> 00:03:12,970
and I think I'll get something for dessert there.

58
00:03:12,970 --> 00:03:14,640
Leon: How about a mango?

59
00:03:14,640 --> 00:03:18,220
Shannon: I'm not sure - they're not always ripe

60
00:03:18,500 --> 00:03:21,630
I'd prefer a melon - it's bigger too.

61
00:03:21,630 --> 00:03:31,030
Leon: Good idea. The owner also sells a lot of spices there that you can put in a curry, and things like coconut.

62
00:03:31,030 --> 00:03:34,340
Shannon: Oh, that's very helpful. I'll have a look.

63
00:03:34,340 --> 00:03:35,630
Leon: No problem.

64
00:03:35,630 --> 00:03:38,540
Shannon: I know bread doesn't really go with curry

65
00:03:38,540 --> 00:03:41,490
but I always like to have some in case.

66
00:03:41,490 --> 00:03:46,540
Leon: As I said - all the bread is home-made and there's lots of variety

67
00:03:47,200 --> 00:03:49,140
I like the brown bread myself.

68
00:03:49,140 --> 00:03:51,220
Shannon: Mm, sounds good.

69
00:03:51,220 --> 00:03:53,370
Leon: They sell other things there too.

70
00:03:53,370 --> 00:03:57,080
Shannon: Like cakes? I love chocolate cake.

71
00:03:57,080 --> 00:04:01,780
Leon: Well - not that, but they have a whole range of tarts

72
00:04:02,300 --> 00:04:05,720
and the best are the strawberry ones.

73
00:04:05,720 --> 00:04:11,540
Shannon: Perfect - hopefully I won't even have to go to the supermarket!
